e against ectopic pregnancy as the source of hemodynamic instability?", "summary": "Lack of vaginal bleeding or pelvic findings reduces the likelihood of ectopic pregnancy as the primary cause."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the sudden worsening of right upper quadrant pain during exercise contradict hepatic vascular occlusion as a cause of hypotension?", "summary": "Acute exacerbation during exercise is less typical for hepatic vascular occlusion, which usually presents with insidious onset."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of fever, jaundice, or leukocytosis disfavor biliary obstruction with cholangitis as the cause of hemodynamic instability?", "summary": "Classic signs of cholangitis (fever, jaundice) are missing, strongly disfavoring this explanation."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of epigastric pain or back radiation disfavor acute pancreatitis as the cause of hypotension?", "summary": "Lack of typical pancreatitis symptoms like epigastric pain and back radiation further reduces its likelihood."}], "differential_history": [], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Hypotension (80/40 mmHg) and tachycardia (110 bpm) with severe right upper quadrant pain suggest hemodynamic instability, potentially due to ruptured ectopic pregnancy (option A) or Budd-Chiari syndrome (option C), both requiring urgent intervention.", "required_actions": ["Initiate aggressive fluid resuscitation", "Prepare for urgent imaging (e.g., ultrasound/CT) to assess for intra-abdominal bleeding or hepatic vein thrombosis", "Administer blood products if hemoglobin is low"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": ""}, "turn_budget_used": 0, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.85, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.0, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of